/* Câu hỏi các đề Tiếng Anh lớp 12 có sẵn. Danh mục (tên, khối, môn, số phút, số câu): data/banks/index.js.
   App chỉ tải file này khi mở một đề trong đó. Dạng câu hỏi: xem đầu data/banks/index.js. */
window.ONTAP_SEED_QUESTIONS = Object.assign(window.ONTAP_SEED_QUESTIONS || {}, {
  /* ---------- Tiếng Anh 12 · Kiểm tra cuối học kì I (Global Success 12, Units 1–5, Review 1, 2; Phiên N12-ck1-ta) ----------
     Sách in năm 2026 (G3HHZA002a26, OnUp-Book lop-12/tieng-anh-12). Từ, mẫu câu, âm theo Book map (tr. 4–7) và các trang của từng
     Unit: Unit 1 Life Stories We Admire (phrases related to life stories; nguyên âm đôi /eɪ/, /əʊ/; past simple vs. past continuous);
     Unit 2 A Multicultural World (cultural diversity; /ɔɪ/, /aɪ/, /aʊ/; articles); Unit 3 Green Living (green living; /ɪə/, /eə/,
     /ʊə/; verbs with prepositions, relative clauses referring to a whole sentence); Unit 4 Urbanisation (urbanisation; unstressed
     words in connected speech; present perfect (the first time…, the most … ever), double comparatives); Unit 5 The World of Work
     (work; stressing auxiliary and modal verbs; simple, compound and complex sentences). Pronunciation hỏi nguyên âm đôi của Unit 1–3
     và trọng âm trong câu của Unit 4 (từ ngữ pháp không nhấn), Unit 5 (trợ động từ, động từ khuyết thiếu được nhấn): Book map của
     Units 1–5 không dạy trọng âm từ.
     Không có câu nghe, không có câu tự luận. Câu, đoạn điền và bài đọc tự soạn, không dùng ví dụ, bài tập, bài đọc, bài nghe của
     sách. Mỗi đề 25 câu chia đúng ma trận 10 Biết, 8 Hiểu, 7 Vận dụng (ma trận ở data/banks/index.js): Pronunciation 2, Unit 1, 2, 3
     mỗi Unit 3, Unit 4, 5 mỗi Unit 4 (trọng tâm; hai câu Biết là từ vựng), Cloze một đoạn điền 3 chỗ trống mức 1-2-3, Reading một bài
     đọc 3 câu mức 1-2-3 dài hơn bài đọc của đề lớp 9; câu riêng của đề ngẫu nhiên chia như một đề thứ ba. Dạng câu của đề thi tốt
     nghiệp: đoạn điền (Cloze), sắp xếp câu thành đoạn văn, thư (mỗi đề một câu, ở ô Vận dụng của Unit 1, 5, 4), bài đọc dài. Cách xếp
     mức: nhận ra từ theo nghĩa, âm, chọn dạng theo dấu hiệu rõ là Biết; chọn thì, mạo từ, giới từ đi với động từ, so sánh kép, liên
     từ, nhận ra loại câu, từ không nhấn là Hiểu; tìm lỗi sai, chọn câu đồng nghĩa, nối hai câu, sắp xếp, chọn liên từ theo ý của
     đoạn là Vận dụng. Ô rút 2 câu (Biết của Unit 4, 5) chỉ có từ vựng; mỗi điểm ngữ pháp của Unit 4 ở một ô (so sánh kép ở Hiểu, hiện
     tại hoàn thành ở Vận dụng). Địa danh theo sách in năm 2026: không ghi tỉnh đã sáp nhập, không ghi quận, huyện. */
  "ta12-ck1-de1": {
    note: "Global Success 12, Units 1–5 (Review 1, 2): Life Stories We Admire, A Multicultural World, Green Living, Urbanisation, The World of Work, with more questions on Units 4–5. Pronunciation, vocabulary, grammar, a cloze text and a reading text. No listening. Every question has an explanation. From the 2026–2027 school year, the Department of Education of each province gives a common end-of-term test in some Grade 12 subjects; check the Department's notice for the subjects and the test format.",
    passages: {
      "green-swap": {
        title: "Read the text. Choose the best option for each numbered blank.",
        text: "GREEN SWAP DAY\nDo you have clothes, books or toys that you never use? Don't throw them in the bin! Our Green Swap Day takes place (1) ___ Saturday morning in the school hall. You can exchange your things for something you need, (2) ___ helps cut waste and saves everyone money. (3) ___, every student who brings at least five items will get a free cloth bag. Anything left at the end of the day will go to a children's shelter in our ward.\nGreen Club, Class 12A1"
      },
      "roof-garden": {
        title: "Read the text. Then answer the questions.",
        text: "Five years ago, the roof of the Sunrise Apartments in Da Nang was an empty concrete space. Today it is full of vegetable beds, fruit trees and even a small fish pond. The project was started by Mr Hoang Duc Anh, a retired engineer who lives on the eighth floor.\nAt first, many of his neighbours did not like the idea. They worried that the soil would be too heavy for the building and that the plants would die in the hot sun. Mr Anh asked a friend who designs buildings to check the roof, and he grew everything in light boxes made from recycled plastic instead of heavy pots. He also built a system that collects rainwater, so the garden almost never needs tap water.\nNow about forty families look after the garden together. They grow herbs, tomatoes, morning glory and chillies without chemicals, and each family takes home a basket of vegetables every week. Scraps from their kitchens are turned into natural fertiliser for the plants.\nThe garden has brought other benefits too. The top floor is cooler in summer, and children who used to spend all their free time on their phones now help to water the plants after school. “We used to live next to each other without even saying hello,” says Mrs Lan, who lives on the third floor. “Now we feel like one big family.”\nMr Anh hopes that other apartment buildings in the city will follow his example. “You don't need a farm to grow your own food,” he says. “You just need a roof and good neighbours.”"
      }
    },
    questions: [
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word has the sound /eɪ/?", o: ["steak", "steam", "stem", "stack"], x: "Steak /steɪk/ has the sound /eɪ/: here the letters ea are pronounced /eɪ/. Steam has /iː/, stem has /e/ and stack has /æ/.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word in this sentence is usually NOT stressed in connected speech? “The old market has become a modern shopping centre.”", o: ["has", "market", "modern", "become"], x: "Here has is an auxiliary verb, a grammatical word, so it is usually not stressed. Market, modern and become are content words, so we stress them.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "mc", q: "My grandfather ___ the village school for only three years because his family needed him to help on the farm.", o: ["attended", "admired", "devoted", "defeated"], x: "To attend school means to go to school regularly as a student.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "mc", q: "When the fire alarm ___, the students were taking a maths test.", o: ["rang", "was ringing", "rings", "has rung"], x: "The alarm ringing is the short action that interrupted the longer one (were taking a test), so we use the past simple: rang.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "order", q: "Put the sentences in the correct order to make a paragraph.", o: ["Pham Van Long was born in 1948 in a small village near Hue.", "After finishing school, he trained to become a teacher in Ha Noi.", "In 1975, he went back to his village and opened its first library.", "He spent the rest of his life collecting books for the local children.", "After his death in 2010, the library was named after him."], x: "The paragraph follows his life in time order: his birth, his training, his return in 1975, the rest of his life and what happened after his death.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "Hue is famous for its royal ___, which includes many small dishes that are beautifully decorated.", o: ["cuisine", "costume", "custom", "identity"], x: "Cuisine means the kind of food of a place and the way it is cooked: Hue royal cuisine.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "tf4", q: "Is each sentence grammatically correct?", o: ["My brother is learning to play the violin.", "Our ship sailed across Indian Ocean.", "Elephants are very intelligent animals.", "My cousin has lived in the Philippines for two years."], a: [true, false, true, true], x: "True: we use the with musical instruments. False: oceans take the, so: across the Indian Ocean. True: a plural noun used in a general way has no article. True: countries with plural names take the: the Philippines.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “Last summer my uncle travelled to the Japan and climbed Mount Fuji.”", o: ["the Japan", "Last summer", "my uncle travelled", "climbed Mount Fuji"], x: "Most country names have no article: travelled to Japan. A single mountain such as Mount Fuji has no article either.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "mc", q: "Most of the rubbish from our city ends up in a huge ___ outside the town, where it is buried under the ground.", o: ["landfill", "container", "compost", "packaging"], x: "A landfill is a place where rubbish is put into big holes and covered with soil.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "fill", q: "Fill in the blank with one word. The shop manager apologised ___ wrapping our fruit in so much plastic.", ans: ["for"], x: "We say apologise for (doing) something: apologised for wrapping our fruit in so much plastic.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence that best combines the two sentences: “Our school has banned plastic straws. This has reduced the amount of rubbish in the canteen.”", o: ["Our school has banned plastic straws, which has reduced the amount of rubbish in the canteen.", "Our school has banned plastic straws, that has reduced the amount of rubbish in the canteen.", "Our school has banned plastic straws, and which has reduced the amount of rubbish in the canteen.", "Our school has banned plastic straws which has reduced the amount of rubbish in the canteen."], x: "Which after a comma can refer to the whole idea of the clause before it: the ban has reduced the rubbish. We cannot use that after a comma.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "Rents in the city centre are so high that many young workers cannot ___ to live there.", o: ["afford", "expand", "decrease", "provide"], x: "If you can afford something, you have enough money to pay for it.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "The roads are always jammed during the ___, when most people are going to work or coming home.", o: ["rush hour", "high season", "short term", "open air"], x: "Rush hour is the busy time of day when many people travel to or from work.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "Since the new factories opened, the streets in our town have been getting ___.", o: ["more and more crowded", "crowded and crowded", "the more crowded", "more crowded and more crowded"], x: "Adjectives such as crowded use more, so we show a change with more and more + adjective: more and more crowded.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “This is the first time my grandmother takes the metro, so she feels a bit nervous.”", o: ["takes the metro", "This is the first time", "my grandmother", "feels a bit nervous"], x: "After This is the first time, we use the present perfect: This is the first time my grandmother has taken the metro.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "At the end of the year, the company gave every worker a ___ of one month's salary to thank them for their hard work.", o: ["bonus", "wage", "pension", "loan"], x: "A bonus is extra money that a worker gets for doing good work.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "Nurses at this hospital work in ___: some start at 6 a.m., and others start at 2 p.m. or 10 p.m.", o: ["shifts", "offices", "uniforms", "silence"], x: "When people work in shifts, different groups work at different times of the day or night.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "___ the pay was low, Mai took the job because she wanted to gain some experience.", o: ["Although", "Because", "If", "So that"], x: "Low pay and taking the job go against each other, so we use although to begin the dependent clause.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence closest in meaning: “The job is well-paid. It also offers flexible working hours.”", o: ["The job not only pays well but also offers flexible working hours.", "The job pays well, but it does not offer any flexible working hours.", "The job offers flexible working hours because it pays well.", "The job pays well, so it cannot offer flexible working hours."], x: "Not only … but also adds one more good point: the job pays well, and it also offers flexible working hours.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (1).", o: ["on", "in", "at", "by"], x: "We use on with days of the week: on Saturday morning.", lv: 1, p: "green-swap" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (2).", o: ["which", "that", "what", "who"], x: "After a comma, which can refer to the whole idea before it: exchanging things helps cut waste.", lv: 2, p: "green-swap" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (3).", o: ["In addition", "However", "As a result", "Instead"], x: "The free bag is one more good thing about the event, so we use In addition. It is not a contrast or a result.", lv: 3, p: "green-swap" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What did Mr Anh use instead of heavy pots?", o: ["Light boxes made from recycled plastic", "Old tyres filled with soil", "Wooden boxes from a farm", "Large bags made from old pieces of cloth"], x: "The text says he grew everything in light boxes made from recycled plastic instead of heavy pots.", lv: 1, p: "roof-garden" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "tf4", q: "Read the text again. Is each sentence true or false?", o: ["All of Mr Anh's neighbours liked his plan from the start.", "Rainwater is used to water the garden.", "The families sell their vegetables at a market.", "The top floor is cooler in summer than before."], a: [false, true, false, true], x: "False: at first, many neighbours did not like the idea. True: a system collects rainwater, so the garden almost never needs tap water. False: each family takes vegetables home. True: the top floor is cooler in summer now.", lv: 2, p: "roof-garden" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What can be inferred from Mrs Lan's words?", o: ["The garden has helped neighbours become closer.", "Mrs Lan does not really enjoy working in the garden.", "The families often argue about the garden.", "Mrs Lan moved into the building last year."], x: "Before the garden, neighbours did not even say hello; now they feel like one big family, so the garden has brought them closer.", lv: 3, p: "roof-garden" }
    ]
  },
  /* Đề 2 (Phiên N12-ck1-ta): cùng Units 1–5, cấu trúc như Đề 1 và chia đúng ma trận. */
  "ta12-ck1-de2": {
    note: "Global Success 12, Units 1–5 (Review 1, 2): Life Stories We Admire, A Multicultural World, Green Living, Urbanisation, The World of Work, with more questions on Units 4–5. Pronunciation, vocabulary, grammar, a cloze text and a reading text. No listening. Every question has an explanation. From the 2026–2027 school year, the Department of Education of each province gives a common end-of-term test in some Grade 12 subjects; check the Department's notice for the subjects and the test format.",
    passages: {
      "summer-jobs": {
        title: "Read the text. Choose the best option for each numbered blank.",
        text: "SUMMER JOBS AT BLUE LAGOON WATER PARK\nBlue Lagoon Water Park is looking for friendly young people aged 18 or over to work as lifeguards and ticket sellers from June to August. To (1) ___, please send us your CV and a short letter by 15 May. Lifeguards must be strong swimmers and hold (2) ___ up-to-date first-aid certificate. The pay is not very high; (3) ___, all our staff get free entry to the park for their families during the summer. We also provide free lunches and training on the job."
      },
      "doctor-thu": {
        title: "Read the text. Then answer the questions.",
        text: "Pham Thi Thu grew up in a fishing village on the central coast in the 1960s. Her father was often away at sea, and her mother sold fish at the local market. When Thu was eleven, her younger brother became seriously ill. The nearest hospital was a day's journey away, and he nearly died before the family got there. “That night, I decided to become a doctor,” she later said.\nThu studied hard by the light of an oil lamp and won a place at a medical university in Ha Noi. Life in the capital was not easy. She cleaned offices at night to pay for her books, and she often had only rice and vegetables for dinner. In her final year, she won a prize as the best student of her class.\nAfter graduating, Thu could have stayed in the city, where doctors earned much more. Instead, she returned to her home village and opened a small clinic. For thirty years, she treated fishermen and their families, often for free. She also trained young people from nearby villages to work as nurses.\nThu retired in 2020, but the clinic is still open. Today it has twelve staff, and several of them are nurses she trained. Last year, a journalist wrote a book about her life, and many readers say it has inspired them to help their own communities."
      }
    },
    questions: [
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word has the sound /ɔɪ/?", o: ["loyal", "local", "lovely", "loud"], x: "Loyal /ˈlɔɪəl/ has the sound /ɔɪ/. Local has /əʊ/, lovely has /ʌ/ and loud has /aʊ/.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "In which sentence is the auxiliary or modal verb usually stressed?", o: ["We haven't finished the report.", "We have finished the report.", "They can finish the report today.", "She will finish the report today."], x: "Haven't is a short negative form (have + not), so we say it strongly. In the other sentences, have, can and will are followed by a main verb, so they are weak.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "mc", q: "Winning three gold medals at the Asian Games was an impressive ___ for such a young athlete.", o: ["achievement", "childhood", "marriage", "relationship"], x: "An achievement is a great success that someone has worked hard for, such as winning medals.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "fill", q: "Write the correct form of the verb in brackets. While my mother ___ (cook) dinner, my father was cleaning the windows.", ans: ["was cooking"], x: "Both actions were in progress at the same time, so each of them needs the past continuous: was cooking.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “When the lights were going out, we were watching a horror film.”", o: ["were going out", "When the lights", "we were watching", "a horror film"], x: "The lights going out is the short action that interrupted the longer one, so we use the past simple: When the lights went out, we were watching a horror film.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "In Viet Nam, giving lucky money to children at Tet is a ___ that goes back hundreds of years.", o: ["custom", "cuisine", "trend", "speciality"], x: "A custom is a traditional way of doing something that people in a society have followed for a long time.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "It took us ___ hour to walk around the old quarter of Hoi An.", o: ["an", "a", "the", "– (no article)"], x: "The h in hour is silent, so the word begins with a vowel sound and we use an: an hour.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best answer to complete the sentence (– means no article): “Our class watched a documentary about ___ Egypt and ___ Nile.”", o: ["– / the", "the / the", "the / –", "– / –"], x: "Most country names have no article (Egypt), but the names of rivers take the (the Nile).", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "mc", q: "Our school canteen has stopped selling drinks in ___ plastic bottles, which go straight into the bin after one drink.", o: ["single-use", "reusable", "eco-friendly", "durable"], x: "Single-use things are made to be used only once and then thrown away.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "tf4", q: "Is each sentence grammatically correct?", o: ["We should all care about the rubbish we produce.", "Our class is preparing for the Green Fair next month.", "Many families in my village rely in rainwater.", "The teacher explained to us how to make compost."], a: [true, true, false, true], x: "True: care about something. True: prepare for something. False: we say rely on: rely on rainwater. True: explain something to someone.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "order", q: "Put the words in the correct order.", o: ["My neighbours", "sort their rubbish", "every evening,", "which makes", "recycling much easier."], x: "Which after a comma refers to the whole idea of the clause before it: My neighbours sort their rubbish every evening, which makes recycling much easier.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "When the shoe factory closed, ___ in the town rose sharply because hundreds of workers lost their jobs.", o: ["unemployment", "employment", "pollution", "industrialisation"], x: "Unemployment is the situation when people want to work but cannot find a job.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "The ___ of this street have asked the city to plant more trees in front of their homes.", o: ["residents", "suburbs", "proportions", "concerns"], x: "Residents are the people whose homes are in a place, such as a street or a town.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "___ we leave home, the longer we will be stuck in traffic.", o: ["The later", "Later", "The more late", "The latest"], x: "Two things change together, so we use The + comparative …, the + comparative …: The later we leave home, the longer we will be stuck in traffic.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence closest in meaning: “I have never seen such a modern train station.”", o: ["This is the most modern train station I have ever seen.", "This is the first modern train station I have seen.", "I have seen many train stations as modern as this one.", "This train station was much more modern than I had expected."], x: "Never … such a modern station means that no station I have seen is as modern as this one: This is the most modern train station I have ever seen.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "Teaching children with special needs is hard, but it is very ___ because you feel you are doing something truly useful.", o: ["rewarding", "relevant", "unpleasant", "casual"], x: "Rewarding means worth doing: the work gives you a good feeling because it is useful to others.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "There is a ___ for a kitchen assistant at the hotel, so my sister is going to send her CV.", o: ["vacancy", "salary", "holiday", "celebration"], x: "A vacancy is a job that is available for someone to do.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "tf4", q: "Is each sentence a complex sentence?", o: ["When I finish university, I will look for a job in Da Nang.", "My sister is a nurse, and my brother works as a pilot.", "Because the shop was busy, I worked there every weekend.", "The interview was short; in fact, it took only ten minutes."], a: [true, false, true, false], x: "True: when I finish university is a dependent clause. False: and joins two independent clauses, so it is a compound sentence. True: because the shop was busy is a dependent clause. False: two independent clauses joined by a semicolon and in fact make a compound sentence.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "order", q: "Put the sentences in the correct order to make a letter.", o: ["Dear Ms Linh,", "I saw your advertisement for summer camp assistants on the Green Valley Camp website, and I am very interested in this job.", "I am seventeen, and I have looked after my two younger cousins every summer for three years.", "Moreover, I can speak English well, so I can help the foreign children at the camp.", "I am free for an interview any day next week. Yours sincerely, Tran Minh Anh"], x: "A letter begins with the greeting and then says why you are writing. Next comes your experience, then one more strong point with moreover, and the letter ends with your sign-off.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (1).", o: ["apply", "employ", "hire", "resign"], x: "To apply means to ask for a job by sending a CV or a letter.", lv: 1, p: "summer-jobs" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (2).", o: ["an", "a", "the", "– (no article)"], x: "Up-to-date starts with the sound /ʌ/, a vowel sound, so the article is an: an up-to-date certificate.", lv: 2, p: "summer-jobs" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (3).", o: ["however", "therefore", "for example", "thus"], x: "Free entry is a good point that contrasts with the low pay, so we use however.", lv: 3, p: "summer-jobs" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What made Thu decide to become a doctor?", o: ["Her brother nearly died on the way to hospital.", "Her father worked at a hospital in Ha Noi.", "A teacher told her to study medicine.", "She wanted to earn a lot of money in the big city."], x: "Her brother became seriously ill and nearly died before the family reached a hospital a day's journey away. That night, she decided to become a doctor.", lv: 1, p: "doctor-thu" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "tf4", q: "Read the text again. Is each sentence true or false?", o: ["Thu had a job while she was a university student.", "Thu found a job in Ha Noi after graduating.", "Thu's clinic closed when she retired.", "Some of the clinic's staff were trained by Thu."], a: [true, false, false, true], x: "True: she cleaned offices at night to pay for her books. False: she returned to her home village. False: the clinic is still open. True: several of the staff are nurses she trained.", lv: 2, p: "doctor-thu" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "Which word best describes Thu?", o: ["dedicated", "careless", "ungrateful", "dishonest"], x: "She studied very hard, went back to help her village and treated people for thirty years, often for free, so she is dedicated.", lv: 3, p: "doctor-thu" }
    ]
  },
  /* Câu riêng của đề ngẫu nhiên (Phiên N12-ck1-ta): chia như một đề thứ ba (25 câu đúng ma trận, một đoạn điền, một bài đọc). */
  "ta12-ck1-ngau-nhien": {
    note: "Global Success 12, Units 1–5, like Test 1 and Test 2, with more questions on Units 4–5. Each time you get 25 questions: 10 easy, 8 medium, 7 hard, with one cloze text and one reading text. No listening. Every question has an explanation. From the 2026–2027 school year, the Department of Education of each province gives a common end-of-term test in some Grade 12 subjects; check the Department's notice for the subjects and the test format.",
    passages: {
      "riverside-park": {
        title: "Read the text. Choose the best option for each numbered blank.",
        text: "RIVERSIDE PARK IS NOW OPEN\n(1) ___ the past, this part of our town was full of old warehouses and piles of rubbish. Now it is a green park with shady trees, a playground and a path for cyclists along the river. Since the park opened last spring, thousands of local people and visitors (2) ___ it to walk, cycle or relax in the cool evening air. Please help us look after the park. Put your rubbish in the bins, and keep your dog on a lead (3) ___ everyone can enjoy the park safely.\nRiverside Park Team"
      },
      "remote-work": {
        title: "Read the text. Then answer the questions.",
        text: "When Vu Quang Huy got his first job as a web designer three years ago, he moved to Ho Chi Minh City. He rented a tiny room with two friends and spent almost two hours a day getting to and from the office. “I loved the work, but the traffic made me exhausted,” he remembers.\nLast year, his company allowed its staff to work from home. Huy decided to return to his home town, a small town in the Mekong Delta. He now pays the same rent for a whole house with a garden as he paid for his old room in the city. He starts work at eight, has lunch with his parents and goes fishing with his father at weekends.\nWorking from home has its own problems, though. At first, Huy found it hard to keep work and free time apart, and he often answered emails late at night. He also missed chatting with his colleagues over coffee. To solve these problems, he set clear working hours and joined a group of remote workers in the town who meet once a week at a coffee shop.\nHuy is not alone. A growing number of young Vietnamese are choosing to live in smaller towns while working online for companies in big cities. Experts say this trend could reduce pressure on crowded cities, but only if smaller towns have fast internet and good public services."
      }
    },
    questions: [
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word has the sound /eə/?", o: ["chair", "cheer", "chore", "chart"], x: "Chair /tʃeə/ has the sound /eə/. Cheer has /ɪə/, chore has /ɔː/ and chart has /ɑː/.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word has a different vowel sound?", o: ["flown", "town", "brown", "crown"], x: "In flown /fləʊn/, the letters ow are pronounced /əʊ/. Town, brown and crown have the sound /aʊ/.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "mc", q: "When Hoa heard that she had won the national singing contest, she was ___. She had never felt so happy.", o: ["on cloud nine", "under the weather", "in hot water", "out of breath"], x: "On cloud nine means extremely happy.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "tf4", q: "Is each sentence grammatically correct?", o: ["My sister was losing her phone on the bus yesterday.", "At 9 p.m. last Sunday, we were watching a football match.", "The sun was shining when we arrived at the beach.", "While he walked home, he was seeing an accident."], a: [false, true, true, false], x: "False: losing a phone happens in a moment and is a completed action, so: My sister lost her phone on the bus yesterday. True: an action in progress at a specific time in the past. True: was shining describes the background of the story. False: walking is the longer action and seeing is the shorter one: While he was walking home, he saw an accident.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 1 · Life Stories We Admire", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence closest in meaning: “My aunt broke her leg while she was skiing in Japan.”", o: ["My aunt was skiing in Japan when she broke her leg.", "My aunt broke her leg, and then she went skiing in Japan.", "My aunt was breaking her leg when she skied in Japan.", "My aunt went skiing in Japan after she broke her leg."], x: "Skiing was the longer action in progress, and breaking her leg interrupted it: My aunt was skiing in Japan when she broke her leg.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "When Minh first moved to Canada to study, he experienced ___: everything, from the food to the way people greeted each other, felt strange to him.", o: ["culture shock", "global trend", "national pride", "local speciality"], x: "Culture shock is the confused feeling you have when you live in a new country with a different way of life.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "Which sentence uses articles correctly?", o: ["My sister plays the guitar in a school band.", "We spent our summer holiday in the Ha Noi.", "I'd like to visit a United Kingdom one day.", "Moon looked very bright and round last night."], x: "We use the with musical instruments: the guitar. We say Ha Noi (no article), the United Kingdom and the moon (there is only one).", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 2 · A Multicultural World", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “Thanks to the globalisation, young people can now enjoy music and films from all over the world.”", o: ["the globalisation", "young people", "can now enjoy", "from all over the world"], x: "Globalisation is uncountable and is used in a general way here, so it takes no article: Thanks to globalisation, young people can now enjoy …", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "mc", q: "In our school garden, we bury fruit peel and vegetable scraps. After a few weeks, they ___ and make the soil richer.", o: ["decompose", "contaminate", "rinse out", "pile up"], x: "To decompose means to break down slowly into very small natural parts.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "mc", q: "Whether our school garden survives the summer depends ___ the students who water it.", o: ["on", "in", "at", "with"], x: "We say depend on something or someone.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 3 · Green Living", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “Many coffee shops now give a discount to customers who bring their own cups, that encourages people to reuse things.”", o: ["that encourages", "Many coffee shops", "who bring", "to reuse things"], x: "To refer to the whole idea of the clause before it, we use which after a comma, not that: …, which encourages people to reuse things.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "After work, my parents spend their ___ time playing badminton at the new sports centre.", o: ["leisure", "colonial", "reliable", "urban"], x: "Leisure time is the time when you are not working and can relax or enjoy your hobbies.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "Our village did not turn into a town overnight; it grew ___ over fifty years.", o: ["gradually", "rapidly", "suddenly", "immediately"], x: "Gradually means slowly, little by little, over a long period of time.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "mc", q: "Thanks to new building methods, the apartment blocks in our city are getting ___.", o: ["taller and taller", "tall and taller", "more and more tall", "the taller"], x: "Tall is a short adjective, so we show a change with comparative + and + comparative: taller and taller.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 4 · Urbanisation", type: "order", q: "Put the sentences in the correct order to make a paragraph.", o: ["The graph shows the percentage of people living in towns and cities in Country Z from 2000 to 2020.", "In 2000, just under a quarter of the population lived in urban areas.", "The figure went up slowly over the next ten years and reached 28% in 2010.", "Between 2010 and 2020, it rose much faster and reached 40%.", "If this trend continues, more than half of the population will live in urban areas by 2040."], x: "We describe what the graph shows first, then the changes in time order (2000, 2010, 2020), and we finish with a prediction about the future.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "Working on an assembly line can be ___ because you do the same small task again and again all day.", o: ["repetitive", "flexible", "relevant", "unpredictable"], x: "A repetitive job makes you do the same thing many times.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "During the busy season, the workers have to work ___ and often stay at the factory until 9 p.m.", o: ["overtime", "part-time", "nine-to-five", "from home"], x: "To work overtime means to work after your usual working hours.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "Which sentence is a compound sentence?", o: ["Lan wanted to earn some money, so she worked at a bakery in July.", "Because Lan wanted to earn some money, she worked at a bakery in July.", "Lan worked at a bakery in July to earn some money.", "When Lan worked at a bakery in July, she earned some money."], x: "So joins two independent clauses, so this is a compound sentence. Because and when begin dependent clauses (complex sentences), and the sentence with to earn has only one clause (a simple sentence).", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 5 · The World of Work", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “Because she wanted to save money for university, so she took a part-time job at a bookshop.”", o: ["so she took", "Because she wanted", "to save money", "at a bookshop"], x: "We do not use because and so in the same sentence: Because she wanted to save money for university, she took a part-time job at a bookshop.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (1).", o: ["In", "On", "At", "By"], x: "We say in the past to talk about a time before now.", lv: 1, p: "riverside-park" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (2).", o: ["have visited", "visit", "visited", "were visiting"], x: "Since + a past time shows an action that began then and is still true today, so the present perfect is needed: have visited.", lv: 2, p: "riverside-park" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (3).", o: ["so that", "although", "because of", "unless"], x: "We use so that to show a purpose: we keep dogs on a lead so that everyone can enjoy the park safely.", lv: 3, p: "riverside-park" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "Why did Huy find life in Ho Chi Minh City difficult?", o: ["Getting to work took him a long time.", "He did not enjoy his job at all.", "His room was far too expensive for him.", "He had no friends to live with."], x: "He spent almost two hours a day getting to and from the office, and the traffic made him exhausted.", lv: 1, p: "remote-work" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "tf4", q: "Read the text again. Is each sentence true or false?", o: ["Huy's company now lets its staff work from home.", "Huy spends some of his free time with his father.", "Huy pays more rent now than he did in the city.", "Huy meets other remote workers every day."], a: [true, true, false, false], x: "True: his company allowed its staff to work from home. True: he goes fishing with his father at weekends. False: he pays the same rent. False: the group meets once a week.", lv: 2, p: "remote-work" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What can be inferred about Huy's new life?", o: ["He has more time for his family than before.", "He earns much less money than he did before the move.", "He no longer works for the same company.", "He never feels lonely when he is working."], x: "He no longer spends hours in traffic, and he has lunch with his parents and goes fishing with his father, so he has more time for his family.", lv: 3, p: "remote-work" }
    ]
  },

  /* ---------- Tiếng Anh 12 · Kiểm tra giữa học kì II (Global Success 12, Units 6–7, ôn Units 1–5; Phiên N12-gk2-ta) ----------
     Sách in năm 2026 (G3HHZA002a26, OnUp-Book lop-12/tieng-anh-12). Từ, mẫu câu, âm theo Book map (tr. 6–7) và các trang của từng
     Unit: Unit 6 Artificial Intelligence (words and phrases related to science and technology; homophones; active and passive
     causatives); Unit 7 The World of Mass Media (words and phrases related to the mass media; linking /r/ between two vowels;
     adverbial clauses of manner and result). Pronunciation hỏi từ đồng âm của Unit 6 (bộ từ khác các từ của sách) và âm /r/ nối của
     Unit 7 theo khung Remember! (tr. 90: từ tận cùng bằng /ɑː/, /ɔː/, /ɜː/, /ə/, /ɪə/, /eə/, /ʊə/ đứng trước từ bắt đầu bằng nguyên âm;
     lựa chọn sai không có cặp từ nào như vậy, kể cả cặp không có chữ r như media + nguyên âm).
     Phạm vi theo đề cương giữa kì II của download.vn (Units 6–7); một đề giữa kì II của VietJack có cả nội dung Unit 8, nên note nhắc
     trường đã học Unit 8 đối chiếu đề cương của trường. Không có câu nghe, không có câu tự luận. Câu, đoạn điền và bài đọc tự soạn,
     không dùng ví dụ, bài tập, bài đọc, bài nghe của sách. Mỗi đề 25 câu chia đúng ma trận 10 Biết, 8 Hiểu, 7 Vận dụng (ma trận ở
     data/banks/index.js): Pronunciation 2, Unit 6 8, Unit 7 7, ôn Units 1–5 2 (ngữ pháp của học kì I, như kho Tiếng Anh 9 giữa kì II;
     mỗi câu một điểm ngữ pháp khác các câu của kho cuối kì I), Cloze một đoạn điền 3 chỗ trống mức 1-2-3, Reading một bài đọc 3 câu
     mức 1-2-3; câu riêng của đề ngẫu nhiên chia như một đề thứ ba. Hai Unit cho 15 câu mỗi đề nên ô Hiểu, Vận dụng của mỗi Unit rút
     2 câu (như kho Tiếng Anh 9 giữa kì I): mỗi đề một câu ngữ pháp (Unit 6: câu sai khiến chủ động, bị động; Unit 7: mệnh đề trạng ngữ
     chỉ cách thức ở ô Hiểu, chỉ kết quả ở ô Vận dụng) và một câu khác (Everyday English, nghĩa của từ, dạng của từ, sắp xếp câu); mỗi
     câu ngữ pháp một đáp án riêng; ô Biết chỉ có từ vựng. Dạng câu của đề thi tốt nghiệp: đoạn điền (Cloze, chỗ trống thứ ba có thể là
     cả một mệnh đề), sắp xếp câu thành đoạn văn, thư, hội thoại (mỗi đề một câu), bài đọc dài. Cách xếp mức như kho cuối kì I. Địa
     danh theo sách in năm 2026: không ghi tỉnh đã sáp nhập, không ghi quận, huyện. */
  "ta12-gk2-de1": {
    note: "Global Success 12, Units 6–7: Artificial Intelligence, The World of Mass Media, with two questions reviewing Units 1–5. Pronunciation, vocabulary, grammar, a cloze text and a reading text. No listening. Every question has an explanation. If your school studied Unit 8 (Wildlife Conservation) before the test, check your school's revision guide.",
    passages: {
      "photo-day": {
        title: "Read the text. Choose the best option for each numbered blank.",
        text: "FAMILY PHOTO DAY AT THE CITY LIBRARY\nDo you have old family photos in boxes at home? Bring up to twenty prints to the city library this Sunday. The event is free (1) ___ charge. We will have every photo (2) ___ into a digital file by our volunteers, so you can keep it on your phone or send it to relatives abroad. (3) ___, you can join a short lesson on how to label the files with names and dates. Places are limited, so please register at the front desk by Friday.\nThe Library Team"
      },
      "rice-app": {
        title: "Read the text. Then answer the questions.",
        text: "When Tran Minh Khoa finished university in Ho Chi Minh City, most of his classmates took jobs at big technology companies. Khoa chose a different path. He went back to his home village near Can Tho, where his parents grow rice, and started building an app for farmers.\nFor years, Khoa had watched his father walk along the fields every morning, looking for yellow spots on the rice leaves. By the time the spots were easy to see, the disease had often reached half of the field. Khoa believed that a phone camera could notice the problem much earlier.\nHe collected more than 30 000 photos of healthy and sick rice plants, many of them taken by his neighbours. Then he trained a computer program to tell the difference. Today, a farmer only needs to point a phone at a plant. Within seconds, the app names the disease and explains what to do in simple words.\nThe first version was far from perfect. It often mistook dust for disease, and older farmers found the buttons too small. Instead of giving up, Khoa invited farmers to test every new version and tell him what was wrong. The app now has large buttons and can read its advice aloud.\nMore than 5 000 families in the area use the app, and some of them have cut their spending on chemicals by almost a third. Khoa still spends most weekends in the fields. “An app is only useful,” he says, “if it is built together with the people who use it.”"
      }
    },
    questions: [
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word is pronounced the same as “byte”?", o: ["bite", "bit", "beat", "bait"], x: "Byte and bite are homophones: they are both pronounced /baɪt/. Bit is /bɪt/, beat is /biːt/ and bait is /beɪt/.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "In which phrase can a linking /r/ appear between the two words?", o: ["newspaper article", "radio advert", "video interview", "TV announcement"], x: "Newspaper ends in the vowel /ə/ and article begins with a vowel, so a linking /r/ can join them. Radio and video end in /əʊ/ and TV ends in /iː/, so no /r/ appears.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Our school website now has a ___ that answers questions about timetables and exams at any time of the day.", o: ["chatbot", "microphone", "keyboard", "webcam"], x: "A chatbot is a computer program that chats with users in writing and answers their questions.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "My laptop is too slow to run the new design software, so I am going to ___ it with more memory.", o: ["upgrade", "unplug", "uninstall", "recharge"], x: "To upgrade a computer means to make it better or more powerful, for example by adding more memory.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "In the robotics course, students get ___ experience: they build and test real robots instead of only reading about them.", o: ["hands-on", "second-hand", "one-way", "full-time"], x: "Hands-on experience comes from actually building and testing things with your own hands.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "In this smart home, you can turn off the lights with a simple ___, for example by saying “Lights off”.", o: ["voice command", "fingerprint scan", "text message", "power button"], x: "A voice command is an order you give a machine by speaking to it.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Before the open day, the head teacher had the IT team ___ the old projectors in every classroom.", o: ["replace", "to replace", "replaced", "replacing"], x: "Have + person + bare infinitive (active causative): the head teacher had the IT team replace the old projectors.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "During a talk on home robots, Lan does not understand the word “sensor” and wants to ask the speaker. What is the most suitable thing for her to say?", o: ["Sorry to interrupt, but what's a sensor?", "May I have everyone's attention, please?", "Hold on! You are talking much too fast.", "Excuse me, may I leave the room for a minute?"], x: "To interrupt a speaker politely, we say sorry first and then ask our question: Sorry to interrupt, but what's a sensor?", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence closest in meaning: “A local printing shop designed the posters for our robot club.”", o: ["Our robot club had the posters designed by a local printing shop.", "Our robot club designed the posters for a local printing shop.", "A local printing shop had our robot club design the posters.", "Our robot club got a local printing shop design the posters."], x: "Have + thing + past participle (passive causative) means someone else did the job for us: Our robot club had the posters designed by a local printing shop.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "order", q: "Put the sentences in the correct order to make a paragraph.", o: ["In 2022, three students at a high school in Hue started a robotics club in an empty classroom.", "At first, they had only a few old motors and a laptop from a teacher.", "A year later, they built a small robot that used a camera and AI to sort plastic bottles from cans.", "In 2025, their robot won first prize at a national science fair.", "Now the club has forty members and a lab of its own."], x: "The paragraph follows the club in time order: it started in 2022, had little equipment at first, built a robot a year later, won a prize in 2025 and is much bigger now.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "The charity concert got a lot of ___ after a famous singer shared its poster with her two million followers.", o: ["publicity", "discounts", "homework", "electricity"], x: "Publicity is the attention that something gets from the public, for example through TV or social networks.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "A fair news report gives both sides of a story without ___ towards either of them.", o: ["bias", "noise", "delay", "pay"], x: "Bias means unfairly supporting one side, which makes a report one-sided.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "The final of the singing contest will be ___ live on national TV at 8 p.m. on Saturday.", o: ["broadcast", "printed", "translated", "delivered"], x: "To broadcast a show is to send it out on TV or radio: broadcast live on national TV.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "On her cooking show, the host talks to the audience as if she ___ an old friend of every family.", o: ["were", "be", "being", "to be"], x: "After as if, we use were with every subject for something that is not really true: as if she were an old friend of every family.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Choose the answer closest in meaning to “credible” in this sentence: “For your project, use only information from credible websites.”", o: ["believable", "fashionable", "expensive", "enjoyable"], x: "Credible information is information you can trust, so the closest word is believable.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “The live interview was too long that many viewers switched to another channel.”", o: ["too long", "The live interview", "many viewers switched", "to another channel"], x: "To show a result, we use so + adjective + that, not too … that: The live interview was so long that many viewers switched to another channel.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "fill", q: "Write the correct form of the word in brackets. Before you share a story online, make sure that it comes from a ___ (rely) source.", ans: ["reliable"], x: "Before the noun source we need an adjective: rely → reliable (that you can trust).", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Review of Units 1–5", type: "fill", q: "Fill in the blank with one word. At the science fair, visitors can learn ___ the ways doctors use AI to read X-rays.", ans: ["about"], x: "Learn goes with about when we mean get information on a subject: learn about the ways doctors use AI.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Review of Units 1–5", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence that best combines the two sentences: “Minh was recording a video for his channel. His phone battery suddenly died.”", o: ["While Minh was recording a video for his channel, his phone battery suddenly died.", "When Minh recorded a video for his channel, his phone battery was suddenly dying.", "Minh was recording a video for his channel because his phone battery suddenly died.", "While Minh's phone battery suddenly died, he was recording a video for his channel."], x: "The longer action follows while in the past continuous (was recording), and the short action that interrupts it is in the past simple (died).", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (1).", o: ["of", "for", "with", "from"], x: "We say free of charge, which means you do not have to pay.", lv: 1, p: "photo-day" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (2).", o: ["scanned", "scan", "to scan", "scanning"], x: "Have + thing + past participle (passive causative): We will have every photo scanned into a digital file by our volunteers.", lv: 2, p: "photo-day" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (3).", o: ["Meanwhile", "As a result", "Unless", "For instance"], x: "Meanwhile means at the same time: while the volunteers work on your photos, you can join a short lesson.", lv: 3, p: "photo-day" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What did Khoa use the photos of rice plants for?", o: ["Training a computer program", "Decorating his new office", "Selling them to companies", "Making a calendar for farmers"], x: "He collected the photos and then trained a computer program to tell healthy plants from sick ones.", lv: 1, p: "rice-app" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "tf4", q: "Read the text again. Is each sentence true or false?", o: ["Khoa's father checked the rice leaves for yellow spots every morning.", "Some of the photos Khoa used came from his neighbours.", "The first version of the app worked well from the start.", "The app gives its advice only in writing."], a: [true, true, false, false], x: "True: his father walked along the fields every morning, looking for yellow spots on the leaves. True: many photos were taken by his neighbours. False: the first version was far from perfect. False: the app can now read its advice aloud.", lv: 2, p: "rice-app" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What can be inferred about Khoa from the text?", o: ["He takes the advice of farmers seriously.", "He regrets leaving his job in Ho Chi Minh City.", "He wants to sell his app.", "He prefers working alone to working with others."], x: "He invited farmers to test every new version and tell him what was wrong, and he says an app must be built together with its users.", lv: 3, p: "rice-app" }
    ]
  },

  "ta12-gk2-de2": {
    note: "Global Success 12, Units 6–7: Artificial Intelligence, The World of Mass Media, with two questions reviewing Units 1–5. Pronunciation, vocabulary, grammar, a cloze text and a reading text. No listening. Every question has an explanation. If your school studied Unit 8 (Wildlife Conservation) before the test, check your school's revision guide.",
    passages: {
      "podcast-contest": {
        title: "Read the text. Choose the best option for each numbered blank.",
        text: "SCHOOL PODCAST CONTEST\nDo you enjoy talking about films, music or science? Then this contest is for you! It is open (1) ___ all students in Grades 10 to 12. Work in a team of three and record a ten-minute episode on any topic you choose. Last year's winning episode was (2) ___ popular that a local radio station played it twice. This year there is one new rule. (3) ___ last year, every team must also send a short written summary of its episode. Please send your work to the Media Club by 30 April.\nThe School Media Club"
      },
      "grandma-channel": {
        title: "Read the text. Then answer the questions.",
        text: "Last spring, eighty-year-old Nguyen Thi Lien had never used a smartphone. Today, more than 200 000 people follow her cooking channel, where she makes the traditional cakes of Hue.\nIt all started by accident. Lien's grandson, Phuc, was filming her in the kitchen for a school project when his friends saw the video and asked for more. At first, Lien refused to appear on camera again. “Who would want to watch an old woman make cakes?” she asked. But Phuc promised to do all the technical work: filming, editing and posting the videos.\nThe first few videos had very few viewers. Phuc noticed that most people stopped watching after about a minute, so he made the videos shorter and added English subtitles. He also asked his grandmother to tell the story behind each cake. Those stories soon became the most popular part of the channel.\nNow Lien receives messages from viewers in Japan, Canada and Brazil. Some say her recipes remind them of their own grandparents. Others send photos of the cakes they have made at home. Not every comment is kind, however, and Phuc deletes the rude ones before his grandmother can read them.\nLien earns very little money from the channel, and she says she does not need more. “Every time someone makes one of my cakes, a small part of my family's history stays alive,” she says. “That is enough for me.”"
      }
    },
    questions: [
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word is pronounced the same as “site”?", o: ["sight", "seat", "set", "sit"], x: "Site and sight are homophones: they are both pronounced /saɪt/. Seat is /siːt/, set is /set/ and sit is /sɪt/.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "In which sentence can a linking /r/ appear between two words?", o: ["The reporter asked two questions.", "My phone shows the time and date.", "The robot answered every question.", "We watch the news at home."], x: "Reporter ends in the vowel /ə/ and asked begins with a vowel, so a linking /r/ can join them. The other sentences have no word ending in /ɑː/, /ɔː/, /ɜː/, /ə/, /ɪə/, /eə/ or /ʊə/ before a vowel.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "The art student brought a ___ of her best drawings and designs to her university interview.", o: ["portfolio", "passport", "certificate", "brochure"], x: "A portfolio is a collection of pieces of work that shows what someone can do.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "The coach uses special software to ___ every match and find out where the team can improve.", o: ["analyse", "decorate", "advertise", "cancel"], x: "To analyse something is to study it in detail in order to understand it better.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Our teachers post homework on an online learning ___, and students upload their answers there.", o: ["platform", "playground", "keyboard", "shelf"], x: "A learning platform is a website or an app where teachers and students share lessons and homework.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "To ___ the new smartwatch, press and hold the side button until the screen lights up.", o: ["activate", "uninstall", "recycle", "unplug"], x: "To activate a device is to make it start working.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "fill", q: "Write the correct form of the verb in brackets. Our teacher got the whole class ___ (vote) on a name for our new app.", ans: ["to vote"], x: "Get + person + to-infinitive (active causative): Our teacher got the whole class to vote on a name for our new app.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Choose the answer closest in meaning to “capable” in this sentence: “This robot is capable of reading the labels on more than 500 kinds of medicine.”", o: ["able", "afraid", "proud", "shy"], x: "If a robot is capable of doing something, it has the skill to do it, so the closest word is able.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “Before the long trip, my uncle got a mechanic fix the brakes on his electric motorbike.”", o: ["a mechanic fix", "Before the long trip", "my uncle got", "on his electric motorbike"], x: "Get + person + to-infinitive (active causative): Before the long trip, my uncle got a mechanic to fix the brakes on his electric motorbike.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "fill", q: "Write the correct form of the word in brackets. Thanks to the new app, our science lessons have become more ___ (interact): we can ask questions and get answers at once.", ans: ["interactive"], x: "After become more we need an adjective: interact → interactive (letting people and machines communicate both ways).", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "The singer refused to talk to ___ about her private life, so no newspaper could publish an interview with her.", o: ["the press", "the fans", "the judges", "the police"], x: "The press means newspapers and magazines and the reporters who work for them.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Every morning, volunteers ___ free copies of the city newspaper at the bus station.", o: ["distribute", "manufacture", "memorise", "invent"], x: "To distribute things is to give them out to many people.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Reporters must ___ every number and name in their articles before the articles are published.", o: ["fact-check", "copy-paste", "brainstorm", "download"], x: "To fact-check is to make sure that every fact in a piece of writing is correct.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Nobody reads the evening news ___ Ms Hoa does: her calm voice makes even bad news easier to hear.", o: ["like", "so", "than", "such"], x: "Like can start a clause of manner (= in the same way that): Nobody reads the evening news like Ms Hoa does.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "On the first day of a summer English course, Phong sits next to Linh, a student from another school. What is the best way for Phong to start some small talk?", o: ["Hi, I'm Phong. Is this your first course here?", "Can I borrow some money from you for lunch today?", "Why do you always speak so quietly in class?", "Please move away. I want to sit here on my own."], x: "Small talk is a short, friendly chat with someone we do not know well: say hello, introduce yourself and ask an easy question, for example Is this your first course here?", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence that best combines the two sentences: “The advert was very funny. Millions of people shared it online.”", o: ["It was such a funny advert that millions of people shared it online.", "It was so a funny advert that millions of people shared it online.", "It was such funny advert that millions of people shared it online.", "The advert was funny so that millions of people shared it online."], x: "Such + a + adjective + singular noun + that shows a result: It was such a funny advert that millions of people shared it online.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "order", q: "Put the sentences in the correct order to make a letter.", o: ["Dear Editor,", "I am writing to complain that your news website shows too many adverts.", "Last week, I counted twelve adverts while reading one short article.", "Some of them covered the text, and others played loud music without warning.", "I would be grateful if you could show fewer adverts or offer a version without them.", "Yours faithfully, Tran Gia Bao"], x: "A formal letter starts with Dear Editor, gives the reason for writing, describes the problem, asks for action and ends with Yours faithfully and the writer's name.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Review of Units 1–5", type: "tf4", q: "Is each sentence grammatically correct?", o: ["My cousin is studying computer science at a university in the United Kingdom.", "Last summer we sailed across Atlantic on a large cruise ship.", "The children cheered when an engineer showed them a dancing robot.", "My sister plays piano in the school orchestra every Friday."], a: [true, false, true, false], x: "True: a university (u sounds like /j/) and the United Kingdom. False: oceans take the: across the Atlantic. True: an engineer starts with a vowel sound. False: musical instruments take the: plays the piano.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Review of Units 1–5", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence closest in meaning: “The online course was free, but very few people finished it.”", o: ["Although the online course was free, very few people finished it.", "Because the online course was free, very few people finished it.", "Although the online course was free, but very few people finished it.", "The online course was free, so very few people finished it."], x: "Although + clause shows contrast in a complex sentence, and we do not add but: Although the online course was free, very few people finished it.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (1).", o: ["to", "on", "at", "with"], x: "Open to somebody means that anybody in that group can take part: open to all students in Grades 10 to 12.", lv: 1, p: "podcast-contest" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (2).", o: ["so", "such", "too", "very"], x: "So + adjective + that shows a result: was so popular that a local radio station played it twice.", lv: 2, p: "podcast-contest" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (3).", o: ["Unlike", "Despite", "Instead of", "Apart from"], x: "Unlike shows a difference between this year and last year: the written summary is a new rule.", lv: 3, p: "podcast-contest" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "Why did Phuc first film his grandmother?", o: ["For a school project", "To start a business", "For a cooking contest", "To win more followers"], x: "Phuc was filming her in the kitchen for a school project when his friends saw the video.", lv: 1, p: "grandma-channel" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "tf4", q: "Read the text again. Is each sentence true or false?", o: ["Lien was happy to appear on camera again at first.", "Phuc made the videos shorter because many people stopped watching early.", "The stories behind the cakes became very popular with the audience.", "Lien reads every comment before Phuc sees it."], a: [false, true, true, false], x: "False: at first she refused to appear on camera again. True: most people stopped watching after a minute, so he made the videos shorter. True: the stories became the most popular part of the channel. False: Phuc deletes the rude comments before his grandmother can read them.", lv: 2, p: "grandma-channel" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What can be inferred about Lien's feelings towards her channel?", o: ["Keeping her family's recipes alive matters more to her than money.", "She worries that the channel has far too many followers now.", "She wants Phuc to stop posting the videos of her cooking.", "She is annoyed by all the messages from foreign viewers."], x: "She earns very little but does not need more, and she is happy when someone makes her cakes because her family's history stays alive.", lv: 3, p: "grandma-channel" }
    ]
  },

  "ta12-gk2-ngau-nhien": {
    note: "Global Success 12, Units 6–7, like Test 1 and Test 2, with two questions reviewing Units 1–5. Each time you get 25 questions: 10 easy, 8 medium, 7 hard, with one cloze text and one reading text. No listening. Every question has an explanation. If your school studied Unit 8 (Wildlife Conservation) before the test, check your school's revision guide.",
    passages: {
      "max-robot": {
        title: "Read the text. Choose the best option for each numbered blank.",
        text: "MEET MAX, OUR NEW SHOPPING ROBOT\nFrom next Monday, a talking robot called Max will welcome visitors (1) ___ the main entrance of Green Park Shopping Centre. To use it, log in with your phone number on its screen. You can ask Max where a shop is, or have it (2) ___ you there. Max can only speak English and Vietnamese for now, (3) ___. Our staff will still be at the information desk from 9 a.m. to 10 p.m. every day.\nGreen Park Customer Service"
      },
      "school-paper": {
        title: "Read the text. Then answer the questions.",
        text: "For twenty years, The Bridge was a printed newspaper written by the students of a high school in Da Nang. Every month, the editors printed 500 copies and left them in the school canteen. By 2024, however, most copies stayed on the tables until the cleaners threw them away.\nThe editors decided to try something new. They moved the newspaper online and began publishing short articles every few days instead of one long issue each month. They also added photo stories and one-minute videos, which students could watch on their phones between lessons.\nThe change was not easy. The team had to learn how to edit videos, and some teachers worried that the articles would become less careful. To keep the quality high, the editors made a rule: no article goes online until two people have checked every name, date and number in it.\nThe results surprised everyone. In its first year online, The Bridge had more readers than in its last five years in print. A video on the school's cleaners, who start work at five every morning, was watched by almost every student, and many of them wrote thank-you notes afterwards.\nSome things have not changed, though. Once a year, the editors still print a special issue on paper. “Our grandparents and some teachers prefer to hold a newspaper in their hands,” says Mai, the chief editor. “Online news is fast, but paper still has its place.”"
      }
    },
    questions: [
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "Which word is pronounced the same as “scene”?", o: ["seen", "sign", "sin", "sun"], x: "Scene and seen are homophones: they are both pronounced /siːn/. Sign is /saɪn/, sin is /sɪn/ and sun is /sʌn/.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Pronunciation", type: "mc", q: "How many linking /r/ sounds can appear in this sentence? “Their editor always answers every letter from our readers.”", o: ["two", "one", "three", "four"], x: "A linking /r/ can appear in their editor and in editor always: the first word ends in /eə/ or /ə/ and the next word begins with a vowel. Our comes before readers, which begins with a consonant, so no /r/ appears there.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "The robot at the hotel reception has a ___ face and voice, so many guests think at first that she is a real person.", o: ["human-like", "home-made", "world-famous", "brand-new"], x: "Human-like means looking or behaving very much the way a person does.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Engineers have ___ the warehouse robots to sort parcels by size and weight.", o: ["programmed", "persuaded", "recommended", "advised"], x: "To program a machine is to give it instructions so that it can do a task by itself.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Instead of giving everyone the same homework, the app gives each student ___ exercises based on his or her mistakes.", o: ["personalised", "identical", "handwritten", "international"], x: "Personalised means made for one particular person and his or her needs.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "With a ___ headset, trainee pilots can practise landing a plane in a storm without leaving the ground.", o: ["virtual reality", "noise-cancelling", "wireless", "lightweight"], x: "A virtual reality headset shows a computer-made world that looks and feels real.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "tf4", q: "Is each sentence grammatically correct?", o: ["We had the delivery robot bring the boxes to the third floor.", "My aunt got her broken tablet to repair at a shop near her office.", "The coach had his players to watch videos of their last match.", "Next week, our school will get all the old computers recycled."], a: [true, false, false, true], x: "True: have + the one who does the action + bare infinitive. False: someone else repairs the tablet, so: got her broken tablet repaired. False: have + person + bare infinitive: had his players watch. True: get + thing + past participle: get the old computers recycled.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Choose the answer opposite in meaning to “advanced” in this sentence: “The new phone has advanced features, from face unlock to a built-in AI assistant.”", o: ["basic", "modern", "new", "expensive"], x: "Advanced means new and highly developed, so the opposite is basic (simple, with only the main functions).", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "mc", q: "Which part of the sentence is wrong? “The museum had all the old film posters copy onto its website so that everyone could see them.”", o: ["the old film posters copy", "The museum had all", "onto its website", "so that everyone could see them"], x: "Have + thing + past participle (passive causative): The museum had all the old film posters copied onto its website so that everyone could see them.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 6 · Artificial Intelligence", type: "fill", q: "Write the correct form of the word in brackets. Facial recognition now has many practical ___ (apply), from unlocking phones to finding missing children.", ans: ["applications"], x: "After many practical we need a plural noun: apply → applications (ways in which something is used).", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Messaging apps let us send ___ replies, so we no longer wait days for a letter.", o: ["instant", "ancient", "silent", "distant"], x: "Instant means happening at once, without any waiting.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "The library has made its old newspapers ___ online, so anyone can read them from home for free.", o: ["accessible", "expensive", "invisible", "breakable"], x: "Accessible means easy to reach or use.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "The small bakery has a strong social media ___: it posts photos every day and replies to every comment.", o: ["presence", "absence", "pressure", "permission"], x: "A social media presence means being active and easy to notice on social networks.", lv: 1 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Which sentence has an adverbial clause of manner?", o: ["Our teacher reads the news aloud just as a TV presenter does.", "Our teacher reads the news aloud when the lesson starts.", "Our teacher reads the news aloud because it helps us listen.", "Our teacher reads the news aloud so clearly that everyone understands."], x: "A clause of manner tells us how something is done: just as a TV presenter does. The other clauses show time (when), reason (because) and result (so … that).", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "tf4", q: "A survey asked 200 students in Grade 12 for their main source of news. Social media: 46%; online news sites: 28%; TV: 18%; printed newspapers: 8%. Is each sentence true or false?", o: ["Social media was the top source of news.", "More students chose online news sites than TV.", "Printed newspapers accounted for a quarter of the answers.", "Almost half of the students relied mainly on social media."], a: [true, true, false, true], x: "True: 46% is the largest share. True: 28% is more than 18%. False: 8% is much less than a quarter (25%). True: 46% is almost half.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence closest in meaning: “The website had a lot of adverts. Because of this, I closed it after a minute.”", o: ["The website had so many adverts that I closed it after a minute.", "The website had such many adverts that I closed it after a minute.", "The website had so much adverts that I closed it after a minute.", "The website had so many adverts, but I closed it after a minute."], x: "So + many + plural noun + that shows a result: The website had so many adverts that I closed it after a minute.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Unit 7 · The World of Mass Media", type: "order", q: "Put the sentences in the correct order to make a conversation.", o: ["Mai: Have you seen the video of a shark swimming in the city streets?", "Nam: Yes! My cousin sent it to me last night. Is it real?", "Mai: No, it isn't. A news website says the picture was edited.", "Nam: Wow, I nearly shared it with my whole class.", "Mai: It's always a good idea to check a trusted news site first."], x: "Mai asks if Nam has seen the video, Nam says yes and asks if it is real, Mai says it is not, Nam says he nearly shared it, and Mai gives some advice.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Review of Units 1–5", type: "mc", q: "___ you practise speaking English, the more confident you will become.", o: ["The more", "So much", "The most", "As much as"], x: "The + comparative …, the + comparative … shows that two things change together: The more you practise speaking English, the more confident you will become.", lv: 2 },
      { topic: "Review of Units 1–5", type: "mc", q: "Choose the sentence closest in meaning: “The last time I watched TV was two weeks ago.”", o: ["I haven't watched TV for two weeks.", "I didn't watch TV two weeks ago.", "I have watched TV for two weeks.", "I haven't watched TV since two weeks."], x: "The last time … was two weeks ago means it has not happened since then: present perfect, negative, with for + a period: I haven't watched TV for two weeks.", lv: 3 },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (1).", o: ["at", "on", "for", "under"], x: "We use at with a point or place such as a door or an entrance: welcome visitors at the main entrance.", lv: 1, p: "max-robot" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (2).", o: ["accompany", "to accompany", "accompanied", "accompanying"], x: "Have + the one who does the action + bare infinitive (active causative): have it accompany you there.", lv: 2, p: "max-robot" },
      { topic: "Cloze", type: "mc", q: "Choose the best option for blank (3).", o: ["but more languages will be added later this year", "because more languages will be added later this year", "unless more languages will be added later this year", "so that more languages will be added later this year"], x: "But shows a contrast: Max speaks only two languages now, but more will come later.", lv: 3, p: "max-robot" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "Why did the editors decide to change The Bridge?", o: ["Most printed copies were never read.", "The school could no longer pay for paper.", "Teachers asked for longer articles.", "Students wanted a monthly issue."], x: "By 2024, most copies stayed on the tables until the cleaners threw them away, so hardly anyone read the printed paper.", lv: 1, p: "school-paper" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "tf4", q: "Read the text again. Is each sentence true or false?", o: ["The Bridge was first published online twenty years ago.", "After the change, the editors published articles more often.", "Every teacher was happy with the move online.", "Each article is checked by two people before it goes online."], a: [false, true, false, true], x: "False: for twenty years it was a printed newspaper. True: they published short articles every few days instead of once a month. False: some teachers worried about the quality. True: two people check every name, date and number first.", lv: 2, p: "school-paper" },
      { topic: "Reading", type: "mc", q: "What can be inferred from the text?", o: ["Shorter, more frequent posts won the paper more readers.", "Students at the school no longer read anything on paper.", "The editors are planning to stop the printed issue next year.", "Teachers prefer the videos to the written articles."], x: "After the editors began posting short articles every few days and added videos, The Bridge had more readers than ever before.", lv: 3, p: "school-paper" }
    ]
  }
});
